  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 249 AM EDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nTypical summertime convection pattern with triple digit heat index \nvalues will continue next week. Conditions are expected to flirt \nwith heat advisory criteria through the week, though if an advisory \nis needed it will mostly likely be in the SE portion of the CWA. \n\nFortunately, thunderstorms will be expected each afternoon which may \nhelp ease temperatures during peak heating. There is pretty good \nagreement that afternoon convection will form everyday for the \nforeseeable future, though no strong signal for severe weather \nexists with the limited shear in place. Strength of storms will \nultimately depend on heating. &&",
